WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:11.400
In this lesson, you will learn to write programs that choose between paths with if-else, and combine conditions with and, or and not.

2
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:20.191
If-else chooses between two paths: one when the condition is true, the other when it is false.

3
00:00:20.191 --> 00:00:22.730
Exactly one path runs.

4
00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:31.087
Put an if-else inside the else to test several ranges in order — like grade boundaries.

5
00:00:31.687 --> 00:00:34.661
Booleans are true or false.

6
00:00:34.661 --> 00:00:37.635
AND needs both conditions true.

7
00:00:37.635 --> 00:00:40.609
OR needs at least one.

8
00:00:41.209 --> 00:00:46.791
Test values on and around each boundary: 89, 90 and 91.

9
00:00:46.791 --> 00:00:50.200
Most bugs hide at the edges.

10
00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:56.817
Python uses if, elif and else for the same chain of decisions.

11
00:00:57.417 --> 00:01:01.261
Great work! Let’s remember what we learned.

12
00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:06.409
Now build along, then try the challenges. You’ve got this!
